  "notes": "Kelley School of Business B.S. in Business, Finance major (bulletin 2026-2027). Degree = I-Core prerequisites (43 cr) + Integrated Core block (12 cr) + Finance major (25.5 cr) + IUB General Education + supplemental electives to 120 cr. Finance major (kelley.iu.edu): BUS-F 303, BUS-F 305, BUS-A 310, BUS-A 324 (required); one accounting elective (BUS-A 329 selected); 12 cr finance electives with at least 6 cr at 400-level (F 307, F 335, F 420, F 494 selected). I-Core prerequisite course numbers verified from Kelley Standard Admission 2027 criteria and the BIDS sample plan (kelley.iu.edu); remaining foundations are advisor-guided choice slots per the Kelley undergraduate bulletin (17 I-Core prerequisite courses, 43 cr, for students matriculating summer 2024 or later). IUB Gen Ed: A&H 6 cr, S&H 6 cr (ECON-B 251 counts toward S&H), N&M 6 cr incl. one natural science, World Languages & Cultures. Minimum 2.0 GPA in finance major courses; C- or better in BUS-F 303 and BUS-F 305. All 300/400 business courses on the IU-Bloomington campus.",
